"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[2832],{34278:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"validate","desc":"Coerces an untrusted value to a `Mode`, falling back to `\\"normal\\"`.\\nClient-sent mode strings are an input to validate, never a fact.","params":[{"name":"value","desc":"","lua_type":"unknown"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Mode\\n"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":98,"path":"src/Shared/Modules/RunMode.luau"}},{"name":"get","desc":"The stamped mode, or `\\"normal\\"` if nothing is stamped yet. Do not use\\nthis to branch at controller boot \u2014 see the boot-race note above.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Mode\\n"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":106,"path":"src/Shared/Modules/RunMode.luau"}},{"name":"await","desc":"Yields until the server has stamped the mode, then returns it. Falls\\nback to `\\"normal\\"` if the stamp never lands. Safe inside any\\n`init` / `start`, which Bootstrap already runs on its own thread.","params":[{"name":"timeout","desc":"","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Mode\\n"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":115,"path":"src/Shared/Modules/RunMode.luau"}},{"name":"getResolvingPlayer","desc":"Server only. The player whose arrival resolved the mode \u2014 the first one\\non the server \u2014 or `nil` if the server resolved with nobody on it. It is\\nassigned before the stamp lands, so it is always readable by the time\\n`await()` returns. Always `nil` on the client, which never resolves.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Player?\\n"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":139,"path":"src/Shared/Modules/RunMode.luau"}},{"name":"initServer","desc":"Server only. Resolves the mode from the arriving party\'s TeleportData\\nand stamps it on ReplicatedStorage. Idempotent; call as early in boot\\nas possible.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":175,"path":"src/Shared/Modules/RunMode.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"RunMode","desc":"Which run mode this server is playing: the normal survival run, or\\nArena. Both run inside the same level place \u2014 this is a mode *inside*\\na place, never a place of its own, so `PlaceUtility.isLevel` /\\n`isMain` keep their exact current meaning.\\n\\nServer: the mode is picked in the lobby queue and carried over in\\n`TeleportData`. `RunMode.initServer()` (called from\\n`src/Server/Entry.server.luau`) reads it off the first arriving\\nplayer\'s join data and stamps\\n`ReplicatedStorage:SetAttribute(\\"RunMode\\", mode)`. Attributes replicate\\non their own, so the client never round-trips for it.\\n\\nClient: `RunMode.get()` reads that attribute.\\n\\nAnything absent, malformed, or outside the `Mode` union resolves to\\n`\\"normal\\"` \u2014 a direct join, a Studio playtest, or an old client must\\nnever break.\\n\\n### Boot race \u2014 read this before branching on the mode\\n\\nThe stamp cannot land before a player exists, so it is **not** there\\nwhile controllers boot. `get()` answers `\\"normal\\"` on an unstamped\\nserver, which is the right default for a direct join and the *wrong*\\nanswer for a controller that started a frame early in Arena.\\n\\nAny consumer that branches on the mode at boot must await it, never\\nread-and-early-return:\\n\\n```lua\\nfunction SomeController.start()\\n\\tif not PlaceUtility.isLevel then\\n\\t\\treturn\\n\\tend\\n\\n\\tif RunMode.await() == \\"arena\\" then\\n\\t\\treturn -- or take the Arena branch\\n\\tend\\n\\n\\t-- normal-mode path\\nend\\n```\\n\\n`await()` yields, which is safe here: `Bootstrap` `task.spawn`s every\\n`init` / `start`. Use `get()` only where the read happens well after\\nboot (a render, a click handler, a wave callback) or where a wrong\\nanswer for a single frame is harmless.","source":{"line":54,"path":"src/Shared/Modules/RunMode.luau"}}')}}]);